          ],
          "content": "121"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.409,
            0.138,
            0.588,
            0.157
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "EXERCISE 8.1"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.123,
            0.167,
            0.718,
            0.233
          ],
          "content": "1. In   ABC, right-angled at B, AB = 24 cm, BC = 7 cm. Determine : (i) sin A, cos A (ii) sin C, cos C"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.123,
            0.238,
            0.421,
            0.256
          ],
          "content": "**2.** In Fig. 8.13, find tan P – cot R."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.123,
            0.263,
            0.522,
            0.301
          ],
          "content": "3. If $\\sin \\mathrm { A } = { \\frac { 3 } { 4 } }$ , calculate cos A and tan A."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.124,
            0.306,
            0.515,
            0.323
          ],
          "content": "**4.** Given 15 cot A = 8, find sin A and sec A."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.707,
            0.183,
            0.871,
            0.338
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_8_image_7.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.124,
            0.332,
            0.658,
            0.369
          ],
          "content": "5. ${ \\mathrm { G i v e n } } \\; { \\mathrm { s e c } } \\; \\Theta = { \\frac { 1 3 } { 1 2 } } ,$ calculate all other trigonometric ratios."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.758,
            0.345,
            0.858,
            0.364
          ],
          "content": "Fig. 8.13"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.124,
            0.373,
            0.887,
            0.391
          ],
          "content": "6. $\\mathrm { I f } \\angle \\mathrm { A a n d } \\angle \\mathrm { B }$ are acute angles such that cos A = cos B, then show that $\\angle \\mathrm{A} \\cong \\angle \\mathrm{B}$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.124,
            0.402,
            0.742,
            0.442
          ],
          "content": "**7.** If $\\cot \\theta = { \\frac { 7 } { 8 } } ,$ , evaluate : (i) $\\frac{(1+\\sin\\ \\theta)(1-\\sin\\ \\theta)}{(1+\\cos\\ \\theta)(1-\\cos\\ \\theta)}$ (ii) $\\cot^{2}\\theta$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.123,
            0.452,
            0.728,
            0.493
          ],
          "content": "**8.** If 3 cot A = 4, check whether $\\frac{1 - \\tan^{2}\\mathrm{A}}{1 + \\tan^{2}\\mathrm{A}} = \\cos^{2}\\mathrm{A} - \\sin^{2}\\mathrm{A}$ or not."
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
            0.435,
            0.967,
            0.563,
            0.982
          ],
          "content": "Reprint 2026-27"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.122,
            0.497,
            0.746,
            0.576
          ],
          "content": "**9.** In triangle ABC, right-angled at B, if tan $\\mathrm { A } = { \\frac { 1 } { \\sqrt { 3 } } } ,$ find the value of: (i) sin A cos C + cos A sin C (ii) cos A cos C – sin A sin C"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.585,
            0.902,
            0.621
          ],
          "content": "**10.** In   PQR, right-angled at Q, PR + QR = 25 cm and PQ = 5 cm. Determine the values of sin P, cos P and tan P."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.632,
            0.721,
            0.651
          ],
          "content": "**11.** State whether the following are true or false. Justify your answer."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.169,
            0.655,
            0.561,
            0.673
          ],
          "content": "(i) The value of tan A is always less than 1."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.675,
            0.548,
            0.711
          ],
          "content": "(ii) sec $\\mathrm { A } = { \\frac { 1 2 \\mathrm { s } } { 5 } }$ for some value of angle A."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.16,
            0.714,
            0.719,
            0.732
          ],
          "content": "(iii) cos A is the abbreviation used for the cosecant of angle A."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.16,
            0.737,
            0.503,
            0.755
          ],
          "content": "(iv) cot A is the product of cot and A."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.763,
            0.447,
            0.8
          ],
          "content": "(v) sin $\\Theta   =   \\frac { 4 } { 3 }$ for some angle  ."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.813,
            0.64,
            0.834
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "8.3 Trigonometric Ratios of Some Specific Angles"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.84,
            0.902,
            0.898
          ],
          "content": "From geometry, you are already familiar with the construction of angles of $3 0 ^ { \\circ }$ , 45°, $6 0 ^ { \\circ }$ and $9 0 ^ { \\circ }$ . In this section, we will find the values of the trigonometric ratios for these angles and, of course, for $0 ^ { \\circ }$"
        }
      ]
    }
